    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting the stolen base upside against high-delivery-time pitchers, anchored by **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**. **Trea Turner** (81.27) stands as our highest-rated asset, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Springs and a significant boost from wind conditions and the opposing pitcher's slow delivery, which maximizes his elite sprint speed profile. **Kyle Schwarber** (79.42) shadows him closely; his platoon advantage against the left-handed Springs combined with a stellar .394 xwOBA makes him an ideal anchor in the OF3 slot. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.70) remains a high-floor play despite his lower batting order position, as his aggressive base-running upside is perfectly aligned with the matchup against Singer.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the roster involved **Dillon Dingler**, who finished just shy of the 40-point threshold with a score of 38.84. While his .374 xwOBA suggests he is capable of meaningful production, the negative platoon impact against Gray forced him to the bench to preserve our game caps. Elsewhere, we are leaning into favorable situational matchups for **Hyeseong Kim** (63.21), who benefits from a 100% stolen base projection against a generous matchup, and **Carson Benge** (62.89), whose score is significantly buoyed by a +14% park factor. \n\nWe are monitoring the **Kazuma Okamoto** (56.63) and **Colt Keith** (54.48) spots closely; both are facing tough opponents in McClanahan and Gray, respectively, and are hovering near the marginal start threshold. While their raw talent keeps them in the lineup, they lack the high-ceiling speed factors that define our current offensive identity. With **Christian Yelich** remaining on the IL and **Gary Sanchez** and **Luke Raley** unavailable for tonight\u2019s primary rotation, we are fully committed to the speed-first approach, trusting that the aggressive baserunning of **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Hyeseong Kim** will overcome the challenges posed by the tougher arms on the mound.",
